    L("Speaker", "female", "People ask whether the sounds in documentaries are real. Mostly, yes, but not always recorded at the same moment as the pictures. Footsteps on snow, for example, are often added later by a team we call Foley artists. My favourite trick is that a bag of cornflour, squeezed slowly, sounds exactly like someone walking through snow."),
